# Smoldering Marsh: "This land enters tapped unless you control two or more basic lands." Turn 5 Bot1 controls a Swamp (one
# basic) and a Badlands (the Swamp and Mountain types, but not basic, CR 205.4c): one basic is below the two, so its
# Smoldering Marsh enters tapped - though Bot2, its opponent, controls two basic lands by then. Bot2 with a Swamp and a
# Mountain of its own plays the same land on turn 6 and it enters untapped (positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Badlands
Smoldering Marsh
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mountain
Smoldering Marsh
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Badlands.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Smoldering Marsh.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Smoldering Marsh.Play

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Smoldering Marsh.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Smoldering Marsh.Tapped = false
